KZ3 patch 1138 (SPU pass 114; upstream candidate): runtime/spu/tests/test_spu_lockline_peer.c's racing-write test
(RACE_ROUNDS = 200000) hands off between three threads (main, reader, writer) with bare `while (flag != k) { }` spins.
With fewer CPUs than threads each hand-off waits for the spinner's scheduler slice to end: on the 2-vCPU GitHub runner
t_lockline_peer took ~10 min (locally seconds; under taskset -c 0,1 it ran past 550 s). Fix: the three waits become
RACE_WAIT, a short pause spin (200) then sched_yield / SwitchToThread. Same rounds, same checks (75 passed, 2 failed,
the two patch-1056 expected ones). Not a runtime issue: the runtime code under test does not spin like this.

--- a/runtime/spu/tests/test_spu_lockline_peer.c
+++ b/runtime/spu/tests/test_spu_lockline_peer.c
@@ -51,6 +51,9 @@
  */
 
 #include <pthread.h>
